# Scheduled jobs for this deployment's `cron` service (docker-compose.yml and
# docker-compose.production.yml). supercronic reads this file from `/app/crontab` — see
# docs/reference/ops.md#scheduled-jobs for what each job does and why it is safe to repeat.
#
# `scripts/run-script.ts` gives every entry point here a non-zero exit on failure and closes
# its Mongo connection on both paths, which is exactly the contract a scheduler wants.
#
# Every line below MUST name an existing `npm run` script, and every `reap:*`/`sweep:*` script in
# package.json MUST have a line below — tests/cross-cutting/scheduled-jobs.test.ts enforces both
# directions, since this file is a second place that has to agree with package.json and nothing
# else checks that it does.
#
# Staggered five minutes apart, nightly at low-traffic hours (the container's default TZ, UTC), so
# five jobs each opening their own Mongo connection do not all land on the pool at once.
#
# `sweep:webhook-retries` is the one job below NOT on that nightly schedule — it runs every
# minute, because the sweep interval IS the retry granularity: a webhook retry due in 5 seconds is
# only actually retried on the next minute boundary — see
# docs/modules/webhooks.md#the-delivery-path. A minute-scale query against an indexed
# `{ status, nextAttemptAt }` is cheap regardless of how the nightly jobs are staggered, so it
# needs no offset from them.
#
# No output redirects: supercronic hands each job's stdout/stderr straight to its own
# (`-passthrough-logs`), which is the container's log stream Promtail ships.
0  2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:quarantine
# WARNING: owned by the account module — delete it when removing the module (docs/modules/account.md)
5  2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:inactive-accounts
# WARNING: owned by the orders module — delete it when removing the module (docs/modules/orders.md)
10 2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:orders
# WARNING: owned by the payments module — delete it when removing the module (docs/modules/payments.md)
15 2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:payments
# WARNING: owned by the orders module — delete it when removing the module (docs/modules/orders.md)
20 2 * * * cd /app && npm run sweep:order-effects
# WARNING: owned by the webhooks module — delete it when removing the module (docs/modules/webhooks.md)
*  * * * * cd /app && npm run sweep:webhook-retries
# WARNING: owned by the orders module — delete it when removing the module (docs/modules/orders.md)
25 2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:invoices
30 2 * * * cd /app && npm run reap:mail-spool
